# `\xHH` hex escapes in a UTF-8 String literal decode to the ASCII char
# `0x00-0x7F`. POS pin for the Rust-model `\x` escape (Track B, R40).
# Non-control values only (`\x41`=A, `\x5A`=Z, `\x48\x49`=HI) so the fmt
# round-trip (Track H scope) never bites.
void main():
    print("\x41")
    print("\x5A")
    String s = "\x48\x49"
    print(s)
